course: dictionary
lesson: 1583
title: Chat: talking and typing
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Chat has two main meanings. To chat means to talk in a friendly, relaxed way, like friends at break time or the animals in a story. «The tactful Mole chats about the harvest, apples and cosy winter.» The Mole is not arguing or giving orders. He is talking kindly and easily.
explain: The other meaning is online. «Noah forgot to log out at the library and his account posted «I LOVE BROCCOLI» in a chat.» Words like library, account and posted are the clues. Noah's message was typed and sent on a screen to other people, so here a chat means messages in an app or game.
explain: Chat can also be a noun, as in a chat or chats, and someone who likes talking a lot is chatty. The word also appears in phrases like have a chat, chat online and group chat. When you meet chat, read the words around it, then ask: is this a talk or a screen?
explain: Online chat needs care. «Real game companies never ask for your password on another website or in chat.» So if someone in a chat asks for your password, that is a warning sign. Only chat with people you know in real life, and tell an adult if anything feels wrong.
fact: To chat means to talk in a friendly, relaxed way.
fact: A chat is a friendly, informal talk, and «have a chat» means talk for a while.
fact: Chat also means writing messages to each other online, in an app or game, in real time.
fact: A chat room or group chat is a place online where several people write messages together.
fact: Online safety: only chat with people you know in real life, never share your address, school or photos, and tell an adult if someone makes you feel uncomfortable or asks you to keep secrets.
exercise: «The tactful Mole chats about the harvest, apples and cosy winter.» What does chats mean here? | Shouts at someone | Writes messages on a screen | Buys food at a shop | *Talks in a friendly, relaxed way
exercise: «Noah forgot to log out at the library and his account posted «I LOVE BROCCOLI» in a chat.» Where did the message appear? | In a letter sent by post | In a school newspaper | *In an online chat | On a poster in the library
exercise: Someone in a game chat asks you to keep a secret from your family. What should you do? | Ask them for their password | *Tell an adult straight away | Send them your home address | Keep the secret and say nothing
test: Which word describes someone who likes to talk a lot? | *Chatty | Shy | Grumpy | Silent
test: «Real game companies never ask for your password on another website or in chat.» What does this tell you? | Passwords are only needed at school | Always give your password when someone asks | *A request for your password in chat is a warning sign | Chat is always safe
exam: What is a group chat? | A talk with only one person | A kind of shop | A quiet corner of the library | *A place online where several people write messages together
